{"id":"int-3152340868e5402a9c8698fff6b1bc31","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-16T22:48:02.191699Z","actor":"Edwin Steele","issue_id":"fps-3jj.3","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"ledger.yaml created + 15 historical claim records backfilled from 10 experiment dirs"}}
{"id":"int-e86f0fd2c29fd095cff57c62d24549a5","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-16T22:56:25.047832Z","actor":"Edwin Steele","issue_id":"fps-1785999730518-9-290db57c","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Won't do — superseded by how shock evaluation actually developed. The 14-fold walk-forward CV already carries shock folds inline (SHOCK_FOLDS = {1,4,9,13}) and every experiment reports a normal/shock regime split, so shock robustness is measured continuously rather than against a separate held-out set. The realised backtest is now the arbiter and is likewise fold-partitioned. A standalone shock test set would add a second, less-used evaluation surface without answering a question the current setup leaves open."}}
{"id":"int-c99525d076b0f0c46a4199800df34ade","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-16T23:14:24.962438Z","actor":"Edwin Steele","issue_id":"fps-1785999730728-11-502a48c1","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Won't do — scope vs payoff. Requires extending snapshot capture, the DB schema and the transformer to carry all fuel types, then backfilling history, before any hypothesis can even be screened. That is a data-pipeline project ahead of a feature experiment, and the owner has decided it will not be reached. The underlying hypotheses (diesel as a cross-fuel margin lead, the U91/E10 spread as a cycle-phase signal) are not disproven — if they are ever revisited they should come back as a scoped experiment with the data work costed separately."}}
