{"id":"int-58053a0e36fea4934edb052d48e42406","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-16T23:43:42.830686Z","actor":"Edwin Steele","issue_id":"fps-1785999729915-3-b976f72a","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Superseded — both halves are spent. The DECIDE half was answered by experiment 2026-06-20_leading_indicators: the realised/CpL arbiter ran over 14 walk-forward folds with all arms at tau=0.25 (no operating-point contribution to net out), tgp_delta_7d graduated at pooled Dcpl -0.039 c/L with gains concentrated in the expensive high-headroom folds, and the raw gap station_minus_tgp_cents did NOT graduate (pools better at -0.136 but by the wrong trade — rescues low-headroom calm folds while zeroing vel7's wins in folds 9/10). The PLUMB half is now components 3-4 of fps-1785999729707-1 (gh#271, AIP TGP production path), which is the live bead for that work. The harness wrinkle noted here (run_paired_realised_backtest shares feature_columns across arms) was solved by the ArmSpec.extra_feature_provider seam. Ledger records: experiments/ledger.yaml (tgp_delta_7d and station_minus_tgp_cents entries)."}}
